    "created_at": "2020-07-02T11:05:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-07-02T11:05:54Z",
    "body": "Yes, I've considered trying it for sure, every time I've come across it. However, the usage is high and can't explained only by enumeration of attributes on window, since it's ~1% higher than another useless attribute, `window.offscreenBuffering`:\r\nhttps://www.chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/356\r\nhttps://www.chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/695\r\n\r\nThere is also risk for Gecko in adding it, namely the risk that Firefox gets classified as Safari or Chrome and goes down a wrong code path. If that risk seems too big to bother with this, then we should probably go down the path of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#concept-navigator-compatibility-mode for this.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/652941277/reactions",
