    "created_at": "2020-07-02T18:18:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-07-02T18:18:17Z",
    "body": "> There is also risk for Gecko in adding it, namely the risk that Firefox gets classified as Safari or Chrome and goes down a wrong code path.\r\n\r\nI'd like to look into this part specifically -- I'm not aware of any sites breaking due to us not supporting `clientInformation`.\r\n\r\nI took the files from https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2379#issuecomment-281925798 and ran them through prettier to be easier to look at. Most of them are here (a few were discarded, namely CSS files and HTML docs): \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/miketaylr/clientInformation-files\r\n\r\n(There's some de-dupe work that could be done, but it doesn't seem worth the effort)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
